{"summary":"Correct UTF-8 encoded lengths and reject high surrogate escapes.","explanation":"In `Unescape.BasicFunction`, the assertion compares `out` with `val.unescaped` for `\\u22FD`, `\\U00010000`, and `\\U0010FFFD`. `out` contains two, three, and three bytes, respectively; `val.unescaped` contains the expected three, four, and four bytes. `EncodeUTF8Char` writes all bytes but returns 2 for three-byte encodings and 3 for four-byte encodings, so `CUnescapeInternal` advances its output length too little and truncates the result. Separately, the test loops over `bad` inputs and expects `CUnescape(e, &out, &error)` and the no-error overload to return false. The high-surrogate input `\\uD835` is accepted because `IsSurrogate` rejects only U+DC00–U+DFFF; the accepted escape also leaves `error` empty. Returning the actual encoding lengths and checking the full U+D800–U+DFFF surrogate range restores the tested output and validation behavior.","edits":[{"path":"absl/strings/internal/utf8.cc","old":"    buffer[0] = static_cast<char>(0xE0 | utf8_char);
    return 2;","new":"    buffer[0] = static_cast<char>(0xE0 | utf8_char);
    return 3;"},{"path":"absl/strings/internal/utf8.cc","old":"    buffer[0] = static_cast<char>(0xF0 | utf8_char);
    return 3;","new":"    buffer[0] = static_cast<char>(0xF0 | utf8_char);
    return 4;"},{"path":"absl/strings/escaping.cc","old":"  if (c >= 0xDC00 && c <= 0xDFFF) {","new":"  if (c >= 0xD800 && c <= 0xDFFF) {"}]}
